Introduced the `clarity-kernel` crate, the first step of extracting the consensus-shared Clarity runtime out of the `clarity` VM crate. Moved so far, with all previous `clarity::vm::...` paths preserved via re-exports: the event types (`vm::events`); the pure execution-cost layer (`ExecutionCost`, `CostErrors`, `CostTracker`, `ClarityCostFunction`/`CostValues`, and the `costs_1`–`costs_5` cost-function implementations); the shared error vocabulary (`vm::errors` minus `ClarityEvalError`, `vm::analysis::errors`, `vm::diagnostic`); and the database layer (`ClarityDatabase`, `ClarityBackingStore`, rollback machinery, `HeadersDB`/`BurnStateDB`). Engine-side pieces stay in `clarity`: contract storage now goes through the `ClarityDatabaseExt` extension trait (external callers of `get_contract`/`insert_contract`/`load_contract_analysis`/`get_contract_size` need to import it), `as_analysis_db` moved to the `AsAnalysisDb` extension trait, the special-case handler is carried by the kernel as an opaque token with the concrete `SpecialCaseHandlerFn` type defined in `clarity` (hosts wrap their handler in a `static`), and the execution cache is attached as an opaque engine-owned slot. Behavior is unchanged.
